A stand-in for the app's own Qt/QML tree, used by ci/harbour-check-selftest.sh
and nothing else. None of it is built or shipped.

The selftest copies the real packaging (rpm/, .github/, ci/, Cargo.*) and
lays these files over it in place of the real qml/, src/, icons/,
translations/, harbour-sukkula.desktop and harbour-sukkula.pro. That way it
proves the *gate* -- that ci/harbour-check.sh passes a tree shaped the way
Harbour wants, and fails each rule broken in a copy of it -- without its
cases depending on the exact text of the real UI, which changes every week.
The real tree is judged by ci/harbour-check.sh itself, in the same CI job.

What is here is deliberately shaped like the app: the imports spec §2
allows, the sandbox permissions it grants, the booster's exported main(),
the four icon sizes as real PNGs, and a tests/ and qml-stubs/ tree outside
qml/ whose imports Harbour would reject and the check must not read.
